  "id": "COMPOUND:13623 - PROTEIN:1692",
  "verbalization": "Selgantolimod appears to have a shared mechanism of action with Magnesium levulinate, which in turn targets Protein S100-A8. This relationship is supported by multiple independent pathways, all of which indicate that Selgantolimod acts as a target for Magnesium levulinate, which then influences Protein S100-A8. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, biologically plausible link between Selgantolimod and Protein S100-A8, likely through a common intermediate, Magnesium levulinate. The presence of multiple targets for Magnesium levulinate further strengthens the hypothesis that Selgantolimod may exert its effects via a similar mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of the same or related pathways. The integration of these evidence points supports a mechanistic framework where Selgantolimod and Magnesium levulinate both influence Protein S100-A8 through a shared target, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
